00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:47.390
<b>The Muozinellan army was about to open the 
Ormea Campaign by chasing down the enemy.</b>

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.560
<b>They laid siege to the mountain stronghold using</b>

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:57.900
<b>their first, second, third, and fourth divisions.</b>

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.950
<b>This left the fifth and sixth divisions,</b>

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.570
<b>as well as their main force, the seventh division,</b>

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:06.330
<b>to pursue the refugees fleeing up the highway.</b>

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:09.660
<b>However, the Silver Meteor Stormtroops and the Olmütz army</b>

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:14.170
<b>launched a surprise attack from the supposedly unoccupied second hill.</b>

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.920
<b>Shoot! Shoot! Shoot!</b>

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:17.200
<b>Enemy attack!</b>

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:17.920
<b>How did they...?!</b>

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:27.740
<b>Now!</b>

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:28.310
<b>Yeah!</b>

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.520
<b>Not bad.</b>

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:44.990
<b>Next one!</b>

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.500
<b>Not afraid of being attacked?</b>

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.540
<b>If you're worrying about that happening, guard me.</b>

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:00.260
<b>So they hid some troops on the second hill?</b>

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:04.680
<b>Ludmila Lourie is well-known for her ironclad defense, 
so I thought that's how she'd play it.</b>

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.260
<b>I guess we played right into her hands.</b>

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.560
<b>Our allies have begun their assault!</b>

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.020
<b>We're joining them!</b>

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.910
<b>The fleeing slaves were actually
disguised soldiers! They're attacking!</b>

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.160
<b>They're what?!</b>

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:31.290
<b>Well now, will the gods of war hunt down those pesky horses and dragons?</b>

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:35.630
<b>Or will we be trampled by their hoofs and claws?</b>

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.840
<b>The group of two thousand Kureys thought to be slaves</b>

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:43.590
<b>were actually disguised soldiers from the Silver Meteor Stormtroops and Olmütz.</b>

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:47.680
<b>They engaged the enemy's fifth division together with Tigre's group.</b>

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:52.810
<b>Meanwhile, the actual refugees were hiding in the hilltop fortress.</b>

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:03.900
<b>We've lost everything!</b>

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.860
<b>We were forced to eat rotten food and sleep outside.</b>

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.410
<b>We've been walking for days on end too.</b>

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.450
<b>What more do you want from us?!</b>

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.160
<b>I know how you feel,</b>

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.160
<b>but please,</b>

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.790
<b>will you do this for me?</b>

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.630
<b>It has to be done</b>

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.750
<b>if we want to save even more people.</b>

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.340
<b>But...!</b>

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:24.260
<b>I'll follow the count.</b>

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:30.010
<b>We can't possibly fight them.</b>

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.760
<b>If they were to attack us,</b>

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.600
<b>we'd lose our heads in no time.</b>

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:38.560
<b>But by following the count's directions, we can not only survive,</b>

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.820
<b>but also pull a quick one on the Muozinellans.</b>

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:51.870
<b>We'll do our utmost to protect you.</b>

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.410
<b>Live up to the trust they placed in us!</b>

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:01.590
<b>The fifth division was wiped out!</b>

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:06.130
<b>The enemy's main force is now evading the sixth division and closing in on the seventh!</b>

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:06.920
<b>What?</b>

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:08.340
<b>They can't be...</b>

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:10.800
<b>Dispatch a messenger to the fourth division.</b>

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.850
<b>They are to come here as reinforcements post-haste.</b>

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:17.980
<b>The other three divisions will keep up the siege on their stronghold.</b>

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:18.600
<b>Yes, sir!</b>

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.060
<b>Let them attack all they want.</b>

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.360
<b>We'll wear them out yet.</b>

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:30.030
<b>Mila and Tigre's force closes in on the 
seventh division and Kureys's headquarters.</b>

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.280
<b>The combined forces of the 
Silver Meteor Stormtroops and Olmütz</b>

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:36.410
<b>are giving chase to keep the 
Muozinellan commander from escaping.</b>

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:42.500
<b>But then the sixth division of the Muozinellan army changes direction to go after them in turn.</b>

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.050
<b>Have our flying column move to intercept!</b>

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:47.130
<b>We'll snipe Kureys in the meantime!</b>

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:52.300
<b>The flying column started moving.</b>

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.300
<b>However...</b>

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:01.770
<b>We're at the breaking point, huh?</b>

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:15.450
<b>Having routed the flying column,</b>

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:18.080
<b>the sixth division closes in on Tigre and Mila's main force.</b>

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.830
<b>We're so close!</b>

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:30.590
<b>Nice try, Ludmila Lourie.</b>

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:34.260
<b>Coming after me was quite the bold move.</b>

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:38.890
<b>You may have actually come close to taking my head too.</b>

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:43.940
<b>Kureys deploys the sixth and seventh units of his army to the sides of the Silver Meteor Stormtroops</b>

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:46.610
<b>in an attempt to surround them.</b>

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:52.530
<b>Already positioned at the rear, he moves farther away to distance himself from Tigre's bow.</b>

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:55.530
<b>It's an arrow-proof formation.</b>

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:59.620
<b>Drag Zhcted's legendary war maiden before me.</b>

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:03.420
<b>After all they're directly below the Zhctedian king in terms of rank.</b>

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.670
<b>We won't treat her as a captive, of course.</b>

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:09.050
<b>Instead, we'll welcome her
nicely as an honored guest.</b>

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.010
<b>Very <i>nicely</i>.</b>

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:19.600
<b>I'll go look for more!</b>

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:20.600
<b>Thanks!</b>

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:24.480
<b>Ludmila, I'll do what I can here, so run—</b>

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.440
<b>Shut up!</b>

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:27.980
<b>They may have the slightly larger army—so what?</b>

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:29.180
<b>Do you see me complaining?</b>

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:32.650
<b>I have my pride as a war maiden!</b>

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:38.370
<b>I'm following in the footsteps of my mother and grandmother—no, of all the war maidens</b>

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:41.080
<b>who have wielded Lavias!</b>

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:45.460
<b>If you've got your pride, then I've got my mettle!</b>

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:46.290
<b>Mettle?</b>

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:52.420
<b>I'm Tigrevurmud Vorn. I've learned from my father and many others to be brave!</b>

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.230
<b>That's why I'll fight!</b>

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:57.550
<b>Fine!</b>

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:01.070
<b>Then let's fight together.</b>

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:03.390
<b>I've got your back!</b>

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:04.940
<b>What?!</b>

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:06.690
<b>Reinforcements?</b>

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:11.690
<b>Charge!</b>

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:14.950
<b>Drive off that pack of Muozinellan wolves!</b>

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:17.700
<b>A band of knights coming from the north?</b>

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:20.620
<b>I thought they didn't have any troops left for an ambush!</b>

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.410
<b>It appears those are enemy reinforcements.</b>

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:24.460
<b>Reinforcements...</b>

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.040
<b>Count Vorn?!</b>

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.130
<b>Where can I find Count Vorn?!</b>

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:30.630
<b>Over here!</b>

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.140
<b>My name is Emile.</b>

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:45.980
<b>After being asked to by Count Mashas,</b>

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:49.020
<b>I and the 1500 knights of the 
Order of Perche have rushed here.</b>

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:52.400
<b>We want to assist you in your fight.</b>

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.650
<b>Forgive me for not dismounting.</b>

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:58.240
<b>I, Scheie, and the 1500 men of the Order of Lutèce</b>

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.910
<b>are here on behalf of Viscount Hugues Augre.</b>

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:04.500
<b>We'll now place ourselves under your command!</b>

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:07.540
<b>I am Auguste of the Order of Calvados.</b>

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:12.670
<b>I and my 2000 knights are here to support you, Sir Tigrevurmud.</b>

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:14.170
<b>Auguste...</b>

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:19.010
<b>Well, time to go and mow those dogs down.</b>

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:20.300
<b>Good hunting!</b>

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:21.300
<b>Thank you!</b>

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.520
<b>Do you remember me,</b>

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:26.560
<b>Count Tigre?</b>

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:29.020
<b>There's no way I could not, is there?</b>

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:31.980
<b>As a former soldier of House Vorn,</b>

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.990
<b>I was disheartened that my position as a knight kept me from helping you.</b>

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.410
<b>But then Sir Roland and Sir Olivier of Navarre</b>

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.780
<b>sent me a letter about you.</b>

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:42.870
<b>Roland?</b>

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:46.830
<b>In the letter he wrote that once you fight for Brune and its people,</b>

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:49.370
<b>I should join you as soon as possible.</b>

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:52.330
<b>When Lord Mashas told me about what is happening here, I realized</b>

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:53.250
<b>now was the time.</b>

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:55.920
<b>The same goes for the orders of 
Perche and Lutèce as well.</b>

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:57.590
<b>Thank you,</b>

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:58.760
<b>Auguste.</b>

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:00.550
<b>Lord Tigre,</b>

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.640
<b>you have become a fine man,</b>

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:04.390
<b>just like Lord Urs was.</b>

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:05.850
<b>Now then...</b>

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:16.540
<b>Are you done talking?</b>

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:21.610
<b>Yeah.</b>

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:24.780
<b>I was able to catch my breath thanks to them.</b>

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.240
<b>How about you?</b>

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.330
<b>Want to fall back?</b>

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:28.750
<b>No,</b>

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.370
<b>I can still draw my bow.</b>

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:31.510
<b>Count Vorn!</b>

